  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the higher probability. The individual in the verbal report also focuses on the probability of receiving a non-zero outcome, explicitly rejecting Lottery A due to its 20% chance of yielding nothing. They prefer Lottery B because it guarantees a positive outcome—i.e., it has a higher probability (100%) of a favorable result. The information considered (probabilities of winning something) and the justification (preferring higher chance of winning over slightly higher payoff) align closely with the decision reason. Although the individual emphasizes 'safety' and 'risk aversion,' the core of their reasoning matches the rule of preferring the lottery with a higher probability of a favorable outcome. Therefore, it is highly likely the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
}

